<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barsbay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1438">1438</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as al-Ashraf Barsbay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barsbay was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 1422 to 1438. He imposed state monopolies on the spice and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> trades, raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and in 1426 captured its king, Janus, making the island a tributary of Egypt. In 1427 he bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alanya">Alanya</a> from its Karamanid ruler, though Mamluk control there was short-lived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barsbay.jpg" alt="Barsbay" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barsbay_gold_ashrafi_1422_1438.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
